@meta
id: 17-08
title: Back to the last change
chapter: 17
type: lesson
skills: changelist
par: 72
minutes: 6
vscode: Ctrl+K Ctrl+Q, Go to Last Edit Location
open: order.provider.ts

@brief
`ship` has a typo: the status it writes is `SHIPED`. Fix it.

While you are there, `ship` should also email the customer, the same
way `create` does. The line you need already exists in `create`, higher
up: the `emailService.send` call. Go and copy it. Then come back to the
line you just fixed, put the copy directly under it, and change its
template to `order_shipped`.

Coming back is the point. You will have jumped at least once, probably
more, to find the line to copy. The jumplist would get you home if you
counted right. There is a list that needs no counting, because it
only records places you *changed*, and you have changed exactly one.

@keys
| `g;` | jump to the position of the last change |
| `yy` | yank the line |
| `p` | put it below the cursor line |
| `?text` | search upwards |

@hints
Yanking is not a change. Searching is not a change. After the typo fix,
the only change in this file is the typo fix.
--
`g;` goes to where the most recent change was made, exact line and
column, however far you have wandered since.
--
`/SHIPED` Enter, `ciwSHIPPED` Esc. `?emailService` Enter, `yy`. Then
`g;` `p`, and `f'l` `ciworder_shipped` Esc.

@solution
    /SHIPED<Enter> ciwSHIPPED<Esc>
    ?emailService<Enter> yy
    g; p f'lciworder_shipped<Esc> :wq<Enter>

Alongside the jumplist, vim keeps a *changelist*: the position of every
change you have made in this buffer, newest last. `g;` walks backwards
through it. Nothing you did between the fix and the `g;`, searching,
scrolling, yanking, reading, was a change, so the newest entry was
still the typo, and one press landed on it.

This is VS Code's Go to Last Edit Location, and it is the key you want
when you have been reading for a while and lost your place. It is also
the better key for "back to the thing I was working on" in general:
the jumplist fills up with every search you make while looking around,
but the changelist only fills up when you actually do something.

Two details. `g;` returns to the exact column of the change, which is
why `p` put the line in the right place without a `j` or `k`. And if
you press `g;` when you are already standing on the newest change,
nothing moves; press it again to go one older. The next lesson is
about going further back than one.

@start order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { CustomerProvider } from '../customer/customer.provider';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';
import { EmailService } from '../../infrastructure/services/email.service';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(CustomerProvider) protected customerProvider: CustomerProvider,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
    @inject(EmailService) protected emailService: EmailService,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }

  public async findByCustomer(customerId: string) {
    await this.customerProvider.findOne(customerId);

    return this.orderRepository.findByCustomer({ customerId });
  }

  public async create(args: { customerId: string; total: number }) {
    const customer = await this.customerProvider.findOne(args.customerId);

    const order = await this.orderRepository.create({
      values: { customerId: customer.id, total: args.total, status: 'PENDING' },
    });

    await this.emailService.send({ orderId: order.id, template: 'order_confirmation' });

    return order;
  }

  public async ship(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status !== 'PENDING') {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_PENDING');
    }

    await this.orderRepository.update({ where: { id }, values: { status: 'SHIPED' } });

    return order;
  }

  public async cancel(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    await this.paymentService.refund(order.id);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }
}

@expected order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { CustomerProvider } from '../customer/customer.provider';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';
import { EmailService } from '../../infrastructure/services/email.service';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(CustomerProvider) protected customerProvider: CustomerProvider,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
    @inject(EmailService) protected emailService: EmailService,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }

  public async findByCustomer(customerId: string) {
    await this.customerProvider.findOne(customerId);

    return this.orderRepository.findByCustomer({ customerId });
  }

  public async create(args: { customerId: string; total: number }) {
    const customer = await this.customerProvider.findOne(args.customerId);

    const order = await this.orderRepository.create({
      values: { customerId: customer.id, total: args.total, status: 'PENDING' },
    });

    await this.emailService.send({ orderId: order.id, template: 'order_confirmation' });

    return order;
  }

  public async ship(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status !== 'PENDING') {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_PENDING');
    }

    await this.orderRepository.update({ where: { id }, values: { status: 'SHIPPED' } });
    await this.emailService.send({ orderId: order.id, template: 'order_shipped' });

    return order;
  }

  public async cancel(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    await this.paymentService.refund(order.id);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }
}
